Question 8: Use arr = np.array([4, 15, 8, 23, 42, 16, 7, 30]). Print the values greater than 10, the even values, and the values from 10 to 30 inclusive.

AIM: Searching elements of given array and checking conditions

Code:
import numpy as np
arr = np.array([4, 15, 8, 23, 42, 16, 7, 30])
print("Values greater than 10:",arr[arr>10])
print("Even values:",arr[arr%2==0])
print("Values>=10 and <=30:",arr[(arr>=10) & (arr<=30)])

Output:
Values greater than 10: [15 23 42 16 30]
Even values: [ 4  8 42 16 30]
Values>=10 and <=30: [15 23 16 30]

Explanation:
Key Concept: Condition checking-arr[condition].
